<?xml version="1.0" ?><!-- =================================================================================== --><!-- |    This document was autogenerated by xacro from /bpe/docker/.sim/install/base101_description/share/base101_description/urdf/base101.xacro | --><!-- |    EDITING THIS FILE BY HAND IS NOT RECOMMENDED                                 | --><!-- =================================================================================== --><!-- base101: THE robot.

     One description for every configuration. What used to be two packages of
     near-identical xacro (base101_simple_description / base101_arm_description,
     differing by two lines) is now two arguments here.

       arm:=false   bare chassis
       arm:=true    chassis + one deck-mounted mod101 arm

     The mod101 underlay is only needed for arm:=true. arm.xacro is included
     inside a <xacro:if>, so with arm:=false xacro never processes it and
     never resolves $(find mod101_description) — an armless workspace builds
     and launches with no mod101 in sight. Do not lift that include out of
     the conditional.

     See docs/bringup-restructure.md. --><robot name="base101"><!-- Palette is by material, not by part, so a new link picks its colour from
       what it is made of. Gazebo equivalents are in chassis.gazebo and must be
       kept in step. --><!-- 60x20 extrusion, black anodized: reads dark grey under light. --><material name="extrusion_grey"><color rgba="0.220 0.225 0.235 1.0"/></material><!-- 3 mm CNC aluminium: the base deck and the payload plate. --><material name="plate_aluminum"><color rgba="0.770 0.780 0.790 1.0"/></material><!-- Everything printed: PLA-CF mounts and brackets, TPU bumpers. --><material name="plastic_black"><color rgba="0.075 0.075 0.080 1.0"/></material><!-- Standoffs and fasteners. --><material name="hardware_steel"><color rgba="0.600 0.605 0.620 1.0"/></material><!-- Bare PCB (the link101 carrier board). --><material name="pcb_green"><color rgba="0.055 0.260 0.140 1.0"/></material><!-- Anodised/moulded electronics housings: cameras, the Orin. --><material name="electronics_grey"><color rgba="0.300 0.310 0.330 1.0"/></material><!-- DDSM210 hub motors and the lidar can. --><material name="motor_black"><color rgba="0.050 0.050 0.050 1.0"/></material><!-- Kept for the add-on packages (base101_arm, the parked tower) and the
       mod101 macro, which reference these names directly. --><material name="silver"><color rgba="0.700 0.700 0.700 1.0"/></material><material name="body_aluminum"><color rgba="0.770 0.780 0.790 1.0"/></material><material name="accent_green"><color rgba="0.180 0.580 0.270 1.0"/></material><!-- Shared base101 chassis geometry. Materials, the gz_ros2_control plugin and
     the sensor/friction extensions (chassis.gazebo, chassis.*.ros2control) are
     pulled in by the variant xacros, not here.

     Folded by hand from the Fusion 360 export (see scripts/import_cad_export.py
     for the mesh side of the same import). Everything below is in the export's
     global CAD frame, in millimetres scaled by 0.001, which is why every
     visual/collision origin is just the negated position of its own link.

     base_link sits on the wheel contact plane (CAD z = -81.965 mm), centred on
     the chassis, so odom/nav/diff_drive see a ground-level origin. The rest of
     the tree keeps the exported positions verbatim.

     Camera choice is an argument: the edge bracket takes either a RealSense
     D435 or a Luxonis OAK-D, and both mount to the same face. Whichever is
     fitted, the stable frames are camera_link / camera_optical_frame. --><!-- ================================= frame =================================
